{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And no man shall be in the Tent of Meeting.</b> Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted in the tractate Yoma of the Jerusalem Talmud: even those of whom it is written (Ezekiel 1:10) ״ודמות פניהם פני אדם״ — 'and the likeness of their faces was the face of a man' — they too shall not be in the Tent of Meeting. And how magnificent is the High Priest in this great rank, that even the holy beasts make room for him for his service, so that he may enter before the King and serve Him in uniqueness, for he is 'a messenger of YHWH of Hosts' (Malachi 2:7). And that Sadducean priest who arranged it from outside and brought it in from inside — an angel came and struck him on his face; he was in the courtyard and not in the innermost sanctum at the time he entered to burn the incense." "<b>And likewise</b> we learned in a baraita in tractate Yoma, chapter one: Rabbi Chiya taught, a sound like a voice was heard in the courtyard, that an angel came and struck him on his face, and his fellow priests entered and found the mark of a calf's hoof between his shoulders, as it is said (Ezekiel 1:7) ״וכף רגליהם ככף רגל עגל״ — 'and their feet were like a calf's hoof.' And this happened to him because he did not believe the words of the Sages, who had a received tradition that it is not to be arranged from outside but from inside, the reason being because of the fragrance of the incense, which has its potency at the time of the arrangement; and he wished to act cleverly against the received tradition and therefore he was punished. May the Holy One, blessed be He, deliver us from punishment and reward us for His righteousness' sake."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:01.410603604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}